	quest.094102DDF9D908E0.title: "Iridium"
	quest.0AAD4422D0E4FD6E.title: "Iron"
	quest.0DECDE6AB2514E10.title: "Gold"
	quest.0E36665F9AE529C0.title: "Silver"
	quest.14B17932F51F7DFA.title: "Silken Strings"
	quest.1648A692A807855E.quest_desc: ["If you click and hold a Brush in the air, after a few seconds you will have a chance to obtain a Dust Pile. By gathering and combining a few of these Dust Piles together, you can craft a solid Dust block."]
	quest.1648A692A807855E.quest_subtitle: "From Thin Air to Solid Blocks"
	quest.1648A692A807855E.title: "Brushing the Void"
	quest.1B78D2B4D4542035.title: "Osmium"
	quest.1BB6D03ADBBFC616.quest_desc: ["With your inventory open, hover over the pebbles and press the 'K' key to compress them directly into their equivalent stone block. Also, sifting Gravel with a Flint Mesh is the only stage where a stone generator is not required. The pebbles obtained here are self-sustaining enough to even increase your total amount of Gravel!"]
	quest.1BB6D03ADBBFC616.quest_subtitle: "KKK K KKKKK"
	quest.1BB6D03ADBBFC616.title: "Pebbles"
	quest.1C330C5F59540D79.title: "Lava Generation"
	quest.1E60EADCD5581776.quest_desc: ["By sifting Dust, you can obtain Silicon Dioxide. This compound is incredibly useful, as many mineral materials, such as Gravel, Sand, and others, can be obtained through it. This will allow you to keep progressing in the modpack and securing more Gravel for your setups."]
	quest.1E60EADCD5581776.title: "Silicon Dioxide"
	quest.32A99EEC8B3196F3.quest_desc: ["The Crook increases the chances of dropping saplings from trees and is essential for finding Silkworms. The Hammer is used to smash blocks: break Cobblestone to get Gravel, Gravel to get Sand, and Sand to get Dust."]
	quest.32A99EEC8B3196F3.title: "Basic Tools"
	quest.3CC83FB66A8B4675.quest_desc: ["The Sieve is your primary way of gathering resources. Place a mesh inside it, then right-click with blocks like Dirt, Gravel, Sand, or Dust to sift them. Different meshes and blocks will yield different resources, so always check the recipes!"]
	quest.3CC83FB66A8B4675.title: "Wooden Sieve"
	quest.419F3FA4FA67DFEF.title: "Biting the Dust"
	quest.4353510E41C7B5E6.title: "Gravel"
	quest.436B8DD8B8D5C97E.quest_desc: ["Welcome to the Chemical Era! From now on, by compressing four chemical elements, you will create a chunk. This chunk can then be transformed into a cluster. There are various types of processing methods available, and depending on the process you choose, you can multiply or even triple your resource output."]
	quest.436B8DD8B8D5C97E.title: "Metal Processing Unlocked"
	quest.49FDD64E107C451A.title: "Zinc"
	quest.51F0FFA41BB429D3.title: "Copper"
	quest.53BCDACA3D52AE68.quest_desc: ["It is time to generate lava without relying on conventional methods. Place Magma Blocks in the Squeezer and jump on it repeatedly to squeeze the lava out. Use pipes or buckets to collect it."]
	quest.5503DDB4C77245A6.title: "Platinum"
	quest.552A69EBBE7999D1.title: "Uranium"
	quest.574CFA66C2330223.title: "Diamond Mesh"
	quest.57717FC754C3C309.quest_desc: ["Right-click with the Silkworm on a tree leaf. Wait for the infestation to spread (the leaves will turn white) and then break them using your Crook to obtain String."]
	quest.57717FC754C3C309.title: "Silkworms"
	quest.5A7051F938985E51.title: "Crushed Netherrack"
	quest.5A9893C9755B6717.quest_desc: ["Place a Barrel full of water near or on top of a Mycelium block. The water will ferment and turn into Witch Water. Place sand inside this transformed barrel to obtain Soul Sand."]
	quest.5A9893C9755B6717.title: "Witch Water"
	quest.5C6BC322514D1BB4.title: "Flint Mesh"
	quest.602CF7690A628C58.title: "Getting Wood"
	quest.60CD57FEC0D24174.quest_desc: ["To create Dirt, fill the Wooden Barrel with organic matter, such as leaves, saplings, or apples. After a while, the material will compost and turn into a Dirt block."]
	quest.60CD57FEC0D24174.title: "Fertile Dirt"
	quest.6233D9BB39F5C44D.title: "Mycelium Spread"
	quest.631C1E5B4D630E23.quest_desc: ["Starting from the Iron Mesh, it is highly recommended that you already have a working Stone Generator. Upgrading past the Iron Mesh means pebble production is no longer self-sustaining, as it will only produce one specific type of stone instead of all four."]
	quest.631C1E5B4D630E23.title: "Stone Generator"
	quest.7C65BB78D5441DA3.title: "Golden Mesh"
	quest.7D096089750267E5.title: "To The End"
	quest.7EA100B1451CFC25.title: "Iron Mesh"
	quest.7F8ACD2B78B7840B.title: "Crushed End Stone"
	task.3282F2BD917969B3.title: "compact"
